      "title": "OS Command Injection in io.netty:netty-codec-smtp",
      "description": "Affected versions of io.netty:netty-codec-smtp are vulnerable to Improper Neutralization of CRLF Sequences ('CRLF Injection') / Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an OS Command ('OS Command Injection'). Allows an attacker who can influence SMTP parameters (MAIL FROM, RCPT TO or HELO) to inject CRLF sequences and thereby craft arbitrary SMTP commands that the client will send on behalf of trusted hosts.",
